A||||3||Fierochic88||Wonderful Fiero Weekend||||6||
Z||000000||Fierochic88||06-25-2001||11:27 AM||||I just had a wonderful Fiero-filled weekend!!<P>Friday night FieroNate (who lives close by) stopped over so we could finally meet him and see his very nice 180,000 mile 87 GT.  I sure hope my car looks that good after that many miles!  Nate was also really great and we look forward to having him around more!<P>Saturday morning dawned not so bright but by mid-day the weather looked considerably better.  We were suprised by a visit from SkiTime, Veronica'sGT & Fleabitdog which lasted pleasantly until mid-evening and involved lots of idea swapping and other interesting fiero stuff.  They even took apart my 88 GT steering rack!  (my poor car!).  I think my dad was glad to have others around who understand Fieros!  Matt also appreciated his new horn button Fleabit!<P>Sunday morning started with more Fieros!  I worked on painting my trim for my 86 Coupe while Matt & Jason "3800SC" Haughey worked on his White 85SE.  Midday we decided to take a run to the yards (the second this week!) and came home victorious!  For $10 I got a pair of freshly recovered speaker seats for my 85 GT in the exact dark grey color that I was planning on doing my interior!  We also got many other Fiero goodies (not as good as the Eq Radio I found earlier this week but still great anyways!).  <P>Upon returning home I was going throught my 85 GT and found a phone number of a previous owner!  I gave him a call and found out that he was the one that got my car painted and he still has paint leftover for me to touch it up!  Plus I found out other info on the car!<P>We ended the evening by seeing the "Fast & the Furious".<P>All this was great and hopefully next weekend will be even better with visits from Northstar87 and FieroLisa as we head out to GM Nationals!<P>Jennifer<P>------------------<BR>Silver 1988 GT<BR>Silver 1986 2m4<BR>Cobalt Blue 85 GT<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/jenscar-sig1.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000001||fierobaby||06-25-2001||11:31 AM||||sounds like you had a great weekend!!!! :-) I wish I could find touch up paint for my car :-( lol well love your car!!! :-) hehehe hope You have fun next weekend too!<P>Corinne <BR> <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/uploads/cfiero.JPG"> ||||reg||10
Z||000002||Fierokid87||06-25-2001||11:49 AM||||sounds like our weekend.  You started the weekend with Fieros, We started ours with the Fast and the Furious.  I hope Fierobaby and I can do more with our car.  but unfortunatly my Fiero wont be done till mid-winter.<P>Scott<P>------------------<BR>Fierokid's  Web site<BR>http://www.angelfire.com/sports/sfiero<P>AIM: Fierokid87<BR>ICQ: Fierokid<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sfiero.JPG"> ||||reg||6
Z||000003||Fleabitdog||06-25-2001||12:12 PM||||Jennifer thanks to you and your parents for a great day and great meals. I felt like I was in Fiero heaven all day. Lots of Fiero's and a bunch of super Fiero people. Congrats on your Fiero finds. I did not know Oley was that close. And Thanks to Jason for a ride in his 3800SC. It was the first time I ever rode in a Fiero with anything bigger than a 2.8 and it was awesome!!!! Looking forward to seeing you all at Carlisle. I hope your parents cruise along. Thanks again  Dave||||reg||1
